//:: cases TC_CA_10_InvNotEstablishedSuppressesNested
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-CA-10: invariantNotEstablished suppresses nested branches inside the dead body.
//
// loop_invariant false makes the body dead (cascade from invariantNotEstablished).
// Inside the body there is a branch (if x > 5).  Without suppression, three errors
// would fire: invariantNotEstablished, body deadBranch, and inner-branch deadBranch.
//
// Suppression chain:
//   1. invariantNotEstablished fires → invNotEstablishedFired = true
//   2. body DeadCodeBlame fires → ancestorFiredFn() = invNotEstablishedFired = true
//      → body deadBranch SUPPRESSED, but firedOrSuppressed = true
//   3. inner-branch DeadCodeBlame fires → ancestorFiredFn() = bodyBlame.didFire = true
//      → inner deadBranch also SUPPRESSED
//
// The invNotEstablishedFired suppressor feeds into the body blame, and the body
// blame's didFire then feeds into the nested branch blame via the ancestor chain.
//
// Expected errors: 1 (invariantNotEstablished).
// Body deadBranch: SUPPRESSED. Inner-branch deadBranch: SUPPRESSED (via ancestor chain).
void f(int x) {
    loop_invariant false;
    while (x > 0) {
        if (x > 5) {       // inner dead — suppressed via ancestor chain
            x = x + 1;
        }
        x = x - 1;         // body dead — suppressed via invNotEstablishedFired
    }
}
